      "parameter": "page_write_boundary",
      "value": {
        "page_bytes": 64,
        "counter_bits": 6,
        "crossing_behavior": "wrap within current physical page, overwriting earlier locations; not advance to next page"
      },
      "unit": "byte",
      "conditions": "After control and two address bytes, first data byte plus up to 63 additional bytes fill one page transaction; Stop initiates programming if unprotected. A boundary crossing wraps even when fewer than 64 bytes are sent. Physical pages are aligned at multiples of 64; application must prevent crossings. More than 64 bytes also overwrites buffered data. Sequential-read behavior or 256-Kbit capacity does not permit cross-page writes.",
